# Deny-token digest list for Test-NoProprietaryLeak.ps1
#
# One SHA-256 per line, of a LOWERCASED single token. The guard tokenises every
# scanned file on /[^a-z0-9]+/ and compares each token's digest against this list.
#
# WHY HASHES AND NOT PLAINTEXT
# This repository is public. A plaintext deny-list would publish the very org,
# client and product names it exists to keep out — the guard would become the leak.
#
# WHAT THIS IS NOT
# This is obfuscation, not secrecy. Single lowercase tokens fall to a dictionary
# attack in seconds. It stops a name being *published in this file*; it does not
# make the list confidential. Do not treat it as a secret store, and never put a
# credential here.
#
# ADD A TOKEN
#   pwsh ./scripts/Test-NoProprietaryLeak.ps1 -AddToken 'SomeClientName'
#
# Comments and blank lines are ignored. Order is irrelevant.

